Part of the ResNet-depth follow-up (RESEARCH.md finding 5): after YOLO's own
node-count table showed achieved-% rising with both width and depth with no
pair isolating either, this reuses already-built/quantized classification
models (no new export, quantize, or RAM risk) to check a second family with
different confounds. resnet50 (50 layers) here at 354.6 fps combined @ N=4;
compare against wide_resnet50_2 (also 50 layers, wider -- isolates width at
matched depth) and the already-measured wide_resnet101_2 (101 layers,
28.5% split-4, results/multi_partition_wide_resnet101_2.log).
